ontracts blossoms and augments along the first free vertex found, skipping the vertices of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"earlier failed searches. The matching returned is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"this procedure’s, a documented function of the vertex order and rows. Parallel edges: the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"copy met first. Vertices of a search that fails are skipped by later searches. O(n · m · log n).","type":"text"}],"url":"\/documentation\/matchingmodule\/graphprotocols\/graph\/maximummatching()"},"doc://MatchingModule/documentation/MatchingModule/GraphProtocols/Graph/maximumWeightMatching(weight:maximumCardinality:)-8dxpn":{"identifier":"doc:\/\/MatchingModule\/documentation\/MatchingModule\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/maximumWeightMatching(weight:maximumCardinality:)-8dxpn","abstract":[{"text":"A maximum-weight matching (NetworkX ","type":"text"},{"code":"max_weight_matching","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", the same matching): as the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"integer overload, following NetworkX’s floating-point path (","type":"text"},{"code":"\/ 2.0","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":") operation for","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"operation, so the same doubles give the same matching. O(n³).","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"maximumWeightMatching"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"W"},{"kind":"text","text":">("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"weight"},{"kind":"text","text":": ("},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Edges","preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P5EdgesQa"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Index","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sl5IndexQa"},{"kind":"text","text":") -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"W"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"k