ocols\/Graph\/minimumWeightFullMatching(bipartition:weight:)","abstract":[{"text":"A least-weight matching covering the smaller side of a bipartite graph, or nil when none","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"exists (NetworkX ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"minimum_weight_full_matching"},{"text":"): scipy’s assignment on the biadjacency","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"matrix, rows ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"bipartition.left"},{"text":", columns ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"bipartition.right"},{"text":" in these orders (NetworkX’s","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"columns follow set iteration, so its matching can differ among equal-weight ones), missing","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"edges forbidden, each pair’s lightest copy (NetworkX keeps the last copy on a multigraph). The matrix is never built: memory O(n + m). An empty","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"side gives the empty matching. ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"weight"},{"text":" is called once per edge, in position order.","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"O(s² t), s ≤ t the side sizes.","type":"text"}],"fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"minimumWeightFullMatching"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"W"},{"kind":"text","text":">("},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"bipartition"},{"kind":"text","text":": "},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:15BipartiteGraphs11BipartitionV","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Bipartition"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":">, "},{"kind":"externalParam","text":"weight"},{"kind":"text","text":": ("},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":"."},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P5EdgesQa","kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Edges"},{"kind":"text","text":".